  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 211 PM CDT Wed Aug 19 2026\n\nAs the upper high/ridge amplify Friday into the weekend would expect \nsome very hot temperatures, especially in favored areas. Heat \nheadlines will be needed and will need to monitor and evaluate \nwhether we will need an extreme heat warning for portions of our \nsoutheast and/or PDC in the next few days.  \n\nSome models were wanting to show some convection on Friday as \nconvective temps are reached (and possibly a residual boundary), but \nat this time the thought is this a low prob scenario and will not \nmention it at this time. GFS is showing this pattern to persist for \nthe next 7-10 days with maybe some hints of it beginning to shift or \nbreak down by the beginning of September. So the heat wave will \ncontinue until that time.",
